From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neogram Patchset <patches@neogram.invalid>
Subject: feature/round-video-policy: pick the round video recorder per device, fall back by itself, limit load

InstantCameraViewBase.create asks NeoCameraPolicy which recorder to use: the stock
round_video_camera2_enabled setting when the user set it, otherwise Auto = the server
switch plus device checks (LEGACY cameras, repeated start failures of the new recorder).
BooleanSetting.neo_reset lets the settings page return the stock setting to Auto.
InstantCameraView2 reports the first recording and start errors to the policy, takes the
output size through NeoRoundCamera.outputResolution (480 instead of 360 when the encoder
needs 16-aligned sizes) and lets NeoRoundCamera.configure adjust the session builder
(start camera, 30 fps when the encoder lacks 60 fps or in battery saver and heavy thermal
load, a lighter camera mode then). RoundVideoCameraController starts with the warm/dual
camera switch disabled when the policy forbids it (battery saver, heat, user choice); the
stock capability checks still apply on top.
